Prompt (summary of the conversation):
Help me implement ITN-03, allowing authenticated users to list their own itineraries and view the details of a selected itinerary.

Review my existing controller and service and help address the team leader's feedback. Add dayCount to itinerary listings, reuse the shared GEN-05 pagination helper with a fixed page size of 10, include ordered days with dates derived from the itinerary start date, and return clean API response objects instead of raw MongoDB documents.

Help me resolve Git merge conflicts with the latest develop branch while preserving teammates' changes.

How the output was used:
Used ChatGPT to update GET /api/itineraries and GET /api/itineraries/:id.

The listing endpoint now supports pagination and returns dayCount for each itinerary. The details endpoint includes itinerary days ordered by dayNumber, with calculated dates. API responses were mapped to expose relevant itinerary fields without internal Mongoose properties.

Added Swagger documentation for pagination and retained authentication and ownership checks.

Verification:
npm run build passed.
npm run lint passed with 0 errors and 3 unrelated Airlines warnings.
