Prompt (summary of the conversation):
Help me implement ITN-05 (Ordered Itinerary Days) in the existing NestJS itineraries module.

Add endpoints for creating, listing and updating itinerary days. Validate city identifiers against the seeded reference data, automatically assign sequential day numbers, derive dates from the itinerary start date and enforce a maximum of 60 days.

Help me handle concurrent day creation using MongoDB's unique index and retry logic.

Review the team leader's feedback and improve Swagger request-body documentation, add a 1,000-character limit for notes, return field-level errors under errors.cityId, correct invalid day ID messages and return HTTP 409 when day creation conflicts persist after retries.

How the output was used:
Used ChatGPT to update the itinerary controller, service and create/update day DTOs.

Implemented POST /api/itineraries/:id/days, GET /api/itineraries/:id/days and PATCH /api/itineraries/:id/days/:dayId.

The service assigns day numbers sequentially and calculates each day's date without storing redundant date fields. It validates cities against MongoDB reference data and uses bounded retry attempts for duplicate-key conflicts.

Applied reviewer-requested Swagger decorators, notes validation and improved error handling. Maintained ITN-05 on a separate feature branch dependent on ITN-03.

Verification:
npm run build passed.
npm run lint passed with 0 errors and 3 unrelated Airlines warnings.
The implementation and review fixes were committed and pushed to the ITN-05 branch.
